    "summary": "A jacket / coat, for a child (?); made from many pieces of salmon skin stitched together.  Flared in shape, left side overlapping right (as worn).  High waisted; pleated below.  Blue/black (indigo dyed?) tabby cotton cloth used to pipe curved left edge (as worn).  Oval-shaped areas of skin cut out and covered with separate pieces of skin; worked in a regular way, suggesting decoration rather than mending.  Some rents in skin.",
